{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 13, :comments [{:quotes [{:he "לך מקום", :translit "lecha makom", :gloss "for you a place"} {:he "אלפיים אמה", :translit "alpayim amah", :gloss "two thousand cubits"}], :mechanisms [{:kind :gematria, :a "לך מקום", :b "אלפיים אמה"}], :frame {:text "The biblical cities of refuge (ערי מקלט) absorbed unintentional killers. Exodus 21:13 designates a place for the killer to flee to. Makkot 10a-b discusses the cities of refuge and the Levitical cities, and Makkot 13a teaches that the two thousand cubits surrounding a city of refuge — its migrash — also function to absorb the killer, so that he attains protection immediately upon entering that perimeter.", :sources ["Makkot 10a-b" "Makkot 13a" "Exodus 21:13"]}} {:quotes [{:he "אשר ינוס שמה", :translit "asher yanus shamah", :gloss "where he shall flee there"} {:he "וכי יזיד איש", :translit "vechi yazid ish", :gloss "and if a man acts intentionally"}], :mechanisms [{:kind :other, :note "Semikhah: the verse וכי יזיד איש immediately follows אשר ינוס שמה, linking the intentional killer to the place of flight."}], :frame {:text "Exodus 21:13-14 juxtaposes 'where he shall flee' with 'if a man acts intentionally,' and the latter verse explicitly excludes the intentional murderer from the refuge. Makkot 9b-10a records the procedure: an unintentional killer who enters a city of refuge and then leaves forfeits protection and may be killed by the blood avenger. Makkot 11b discusses whether courts have authority to remove a person from a city of refuge.", :sources ["Exodus 21:13-14" "Makkot 9b-10a" "Makkot 11b"]}}], :arithmetic [{:kind :gematria, :a "לך מקום", :a-value 236, :b "אלפיים אמה", :b-value 217, :lens :standard, :by :selah, :equal? false} {:kind :other, :note "Semikhah: the verse וכי יזיד איש immediately follows אשר ינוס שמה, linking the intentional killer to the place of flight.", :by :selah, :ran? false}], :book :exodus, :voice :baal-haturim, :lang :en, :chapter 21, :discipline "bht-chalkboard-v1", :timestamp "2026-07-12T23:18:00.725345330Z", :model "glm-5.2"}